# PyMolViz testing

Automated tests live in `tests/`. The repo-root `test/` folder holds **exported PyMOL visual scripts** — never run those under pytest.

## Default (always run after logic changes)

```bash
pytest tests/unit tests/runtime
```

Install deps: `pip install -e "module/[test]"`

## Pyramid

| Layer | When | Marker |
|-------|------|--------|
| Unit | Semantic code, no real PyMOL/Qt | default |
| FakeCmd runtime | `cmd`-facing runtime/session code | default |
| Real PyMOL | Live `load_cgo`, session hooks | `@pytest.mark.pymol` |
| Qt wizard | Tooltips, deferred preview callbacks | `@pytest.mark.qt` |

Opt-in: `pytest -m pymol tests/pymol` · `pytest -m qt tests/qt`

## Agent workflow

1. After editing production code, run the **mapped test file(s)** for that area (see scoped rules).
2. Prefer extending existing tests over new one-off scripts.
3. New `cmd.*` usage in runtime → add the method to `tests/fakes/cmd.py` first.
4. Unit tests: stub pymol via `tests/conftest.py` or import leaf modules only; do **not** import `pymolviz.wizard`.
5. Assert token **shapes** (opcode sequences, segment counts), not golden float geometry dumps.
6. No sleeps or `QTimer` waits in unit/runtime tests — invoke callbacks directly.
7. GUI/wizard changes are optional-layer only; keep CI on unit + runtime.
